  "releaseNotes": "6.3.0 — Multi-Tenancy Support\n      - New TenantOptions configuration: set ClaimName to read the tenant identifier from a JWT claim, or provide a custom TenantResolver Func<HttpContext, string> for full control (headers, subdomains, routes, query strings, etc.)\n      - New TenantDispatchBehavior MediatR pipeline behavior: extracts the tenant name from the HTTP context, populates the scoped TenantContext (TenantName + ConnectionString) before any handler runs, and routes to the correct tenant-specific handler when one is registered.\n      - New IMultiTenantHandler interface: implement on any IRequestHandler to declare which tenant it serves (public string TenantName => \"Tenant1\"). Handlers are auto-discovered at startup — no attributes, no manual registration required.\n      - New TenantContext scoped service: inject into your DbContext to apply per-tenant connection strings transparently.\n      - New ConnectionStringResolver hook in TenantOptions: maps the resolved tenant name to a database connection string (e.g. tenantName => configuration.GetConnectionString(tenantName)).\n      - All existing MediatR pipeline behaviors (caching, logging, custom) continue to run normally for both tenant-specific and default handlers.\n      - Fully opt-in: set TenantOptions = null (default) to keep existing behaviour unchanged.",
